{{smaller block|There were five of them — Pell was ''bones.''{{right|''Mayhew.''}}}}
'''8†.''' Half of the stake in the game of bone-ace (which see).—'''9.''' In ''coal-mining'', slaty or clayey portions or partings in coal.—'''A bone to pick''', {{smaller|something to occupy one; a difficulty, dispute, etc., to solve or settle; a cause of contention.}}—'''Angular bone.''' {{smaller|See ''angular''.}}—'''Articular bone.''' {{smaller|Same as ''articulare''.}}—'''Bag of bones.''' {{smaller|See ''bag''<sup>1</sup>.}}—'''Bone of contention,''' {{smaller|a subject of dispute or rivalry: probably from the manner in which dogs quarrel over a bone.}}
{{smaller block|While any flesh remains on a bone, it continues a ''bone of contention.''{{right|''Brooke'', Fool of Quality, I. 249.}}
Sardinia was one of the chief ''bones of contention'' between Genoa and Pisa.{{right|''Brougham.''}}}}
'''Bone porcelain,''' {{smaller|a name given to fine pottery in the composition of which bone-dust has been used.}}—'''Bones of Bertin,''' {{smaller|in ''anat.'', two small, triangular, turbinated bones, often found beneath the small opening of the sphenoidal sinus; the sphenoidal spongy bones, or sphenoturbinals.}}—'''Canaliculi of bone.''' {{smaller|See ''canaliculus''.}}—'''Coracoid, coronary, cotyloid, cranial bone.''' {{smaller|See the adjectives.}}—'''Crazy bone.''' {{smaller|Same as ''funny-bone''.}}—'''Cuneiform, cylindrical,''' {{smaller|etc.,}} '''bone.''' {{smaller|See the adjectives.}}—'''Earth of bone.''' {{smaller|See ''earth''.}}—'''Epactal bone,''' {{smaller|in ''anat.'', the Wormian bone at the superior angle of the occipital bone.}}—'''Ethmoid bone.''' {{smaller|See ''ethmoid''.}}—'''Funny bone.''' {{smaller|See ''funny-bone''.}}—'''Hyoid bone.''' {{smaller|Same as ''hyoid'', ''n.''}}—'''Hyomandibular, marsupial,''' {{smaller|etc.,}} '''bone.''' {{smaller|See the adjectives.}}—'''Navicular, occipital,''' {{smaller|etc.,}} '''bone.''' {{smaller|See the adjectives.}}—'''The ten bones,''' {{smaller|the ten fingers.}}
{{smaller block|By these ''ten bones'', my lords, he did speak them to me in the garret one night.{{right|''Shak.'', 2 Hen. VI., i. 3.}}}}
'''To be upon the bones of,''' {{smaller|to attack. [Rare and vulgar.]}}
{{smaller block|Puss had a month’s mind to be ''upon the bones of'' him, but was not willing to pick a quarrel.{{right|''Sir R. L’Estrange.''}}}}
'''To carry a bone in the mouth,''' {{smaller|to throw up a foam or spray under the bows: said of a ship.}}

readings.c1s3:
{{smaller block|<poem>See how she leaps, as the blasts o’ertake her,
And speeds away with ''a bone in'' her ''mouth!''</poem>
{{right|''Longfellow'', Golden Legend, v.}}}}

{{smaller|'''To find bones in''', to be unable to swallow: in allusion to the occurrence of fish-bones in soup.—'''To have a bone in one’s leg, throat''', etc., to be unable to go, talk, etc.: a feigned excuse.—'''To make no bones of''', to make or have no scruples about, or in regard to. [Now only colloq.]}}
{{smaller block|Perjury will easily downe with him that hath ''made no bones of'' murther.
{{right|''Bp. Hall'', Cases of Conscience.}}}}
{{smaller|'''To put a bone in any one’s hood†''', to break a person’s head, or cut it off.—'''Without more bones''', without further objection or scruple.—'''Wormian bones''', small or irregular bones frequently found in the course of the sutures of the skull. They occur chiefly in the sutures between the parietals and other bones, and are of no determinate size, shape, or number. Sometimes there are none, sometimes several hundred.}}

'''bone'''<sup>1</sup> (bōn), ''v.''; pret. and pp. ''boned'', ppr. ''boning''. [< ''bone''<sup>1</sup>, ''n.''] '''I.''' ''trans.'' '''1.''' To take out the bones of: as, to ''bone'' a turkey, a ham, etc. —'''2.''' To put whalebone into.—'''3.''' To manure with bone-dust.—'''4.''' To seize; make off with, as a dog makes off with a bone; get possession of; appropriate; steal. [Slang.]
{{smaller block|Why you were living here, and what you had ''boned'', and who you ''boned'' it from, wasn’t it?
{{right|''Dickens.''}}}}

